{
    "background_story": "Mina was a young Sikh woman who drew inspiration from the teachings of Guru Nanak, the founder of Sikhism. Growing up in a diverse community, she was deeply moved by his message of equality, compassion, and service to humanity. Mina became involved in various social causes, volunteering at local food banks and participating in environmental initiatives. She was particularly drawn to Guru Nanak's emphasis on the importance of selfless service, and she spent countless hours helping those in need. As she delved deeper into the Guru's teachings, Mina found solace in his words, 'The greatest glory in living lies not in never falling, but in rising every time we fall.' Her faith and conviction guided her to become a beacon of hope and kindness in her community, inspiring others to follow in the footsteps of Guru Nanak.",
